# Blizzard Interface Reference

This repo ships Blizzard UI source under `reference/`. Prefer it over web docs or guesswork for WoW UI APIs, frame templates, events, and unit-frame behavior.

Live client dumps on this machine (read-only, not product code):

- Live retail: `g:\Blizzard Games\World of Warcraft\_retail_\BlizzardInterfaceCode`
- PTR (xptr): `g:\Blizzard Games\World of Warcraft\_xptr_\BlizzardInterfaceCode`

Retail and PTR Interface trees **differ** (e.g. PTR has `UnitFrameUtil` / 12.1.5 AuraContainer APIs; live retail may not). Prefer the dump that matches the **build you are targeting**. Do not assume a symbol in PTR exists on live Mainline.

## Search order

1. **Unit-frame packages** (start here for almost all WhoaUnitFrames work):
   - `reference/Blizzard_UnitFrame`
   - `reference/Blizzard_CompactRaidFrames`
   - `reference/Blizzard_RaidFrame`
   - `reference/Blizzard_CUFProfiles`
   - `reference/Blizzard_SharedXMLGame`
2. **Full interface tree** only if the answer is not in those packages:
   - `reference/BlizzardInterfaceCode`
3. **Live client dump** when `reference/` is stale for that build (`_retail_` vs `_xptr_`)

## Version folders

Addon targets live clients in `WhoaUnitFrames.toc` (Vanilla / TBC Anniversary / Mists / Mainline). When a package has flavor folders (`Classic`, `Vanilla`, `Wrath`, `Cata`, `Mists`, `Shared`, `Mainline`):

- Prefer `Classic` / era folders that match the live TOC, plus `Shared`
- Use Wrath/Cata (or other) era folders only as historical reference when live Classic/Shared lack the symbol — those clients are not shipping targets
- Avoid `Mainline`-only APIs unless intentionally supporting retail/PTR
- Within Mainline, gate build-specific APIs by capability / Interface version (see whoa-unitframes rule: retail vs PTR)

## How to use reference code

- Read Blizzard `.lua` / `.xml` to learn real APIs, templates, and call patterns
- Mirror secure/taint-safe patterns (combat lockdown, unit tokens, attribute-driven frames) on **Whoa frames only**
- Do **not** copy Blizzard files wholesale into the addon
- Default Blizzard frames: **hide + mute events/OnUpdate** (via `Blizzard_Classic.lua` / `Blizzard_Mainline.lua`; Mainline conceals with alpha + mouse instead of Hide/reparent); never skin or rework them — build Whoa replacements instead
- Cite the reference path when explaining behavior (e.g. `reference/Blizzard_UnitFrame/Classic/...`, or `_xptr_\...\UnitFrameUtil.lua`)
